      "message": "I wonder if a a list is the right structure here? Could / should it be a set instead? Lists imply ordering and can support duplicates. Sets don\u0027t.\n\nI think that if you make it a set then you can just use equals() to check if the list has changed?\n\nWhat happens if the upstream LinkProperties have two IPv6 addresses in the same prefix, such as 2001:db8:1::f00/64 and 2001:db8:1::cafe/64? Will the code try to add two rules and fail to add the second one?",
